cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DLPaC: Data Loss Prevention as Code"
message: "If you use this software or build on the DLP-as-code methodology it defines, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Medeiros
    given-names: Jared
    alias: s0undsystem
repository-code: "https://github.com/s0undsystem/DLP-as-Code"
abstract: >-
  DLPaC treats data loss prevention policy as source code rather than portal
  configuration. Policies are authored in a domain-specific YAML language,
  compiled and validated offline into an intermediate representation with
  fail-closed name-to-GUID resolution, and applied to a tenant through a
  reviewable, simulation-first pipeline. The approach addresses a property
  specific to DLP: its failure mode is silent, since a misconfigured rule does
  not error, it matches nothing, making zero alerts indistinguishable from zero
  violations. The reference implementation targets Microsoft Purview.
keywords:
  - data loss prevention
  - policy as code
  - detection as code
  - microsoft purview
  - compliance automation
  - gitops
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
version: "0.1.0"
